* The input/output builtins of the Refal-5 reference, clause by clause (section
* C.1), for the half that needs no filesystem path.
*
* C.1.1  <Card> returns the next line from the input file, or macrodigit 0 at
*        end of file.
* C.1.2  <Print e.Expr> prints e.Expr and returns e.Expr.
* C.1.3  <Prout e.Expr> prints e.Expr and returns the empty expression.
* C.1.8  A file descriptor is a macrodigit; 0 is the terminal, and <Get s.D>
*        acts like <Card> on the file the descriptor names.
*
* The other half of the section -- Open, Put, Putout and Get on a real file --
* needs a path that is valid wherever the suite runs, and a committed fixture
* cannot carry one. Those clauses are bound to the runtime's own test instead,
* which is what the `unit` rows of `examples/builtin-conformance.manifest` name.
*
* The suite runs the program with its standard input closed, so Card and Get 0
* both see end of file immediately and return macrodigit 0, which is exactly the
* behaviour C.1.1 specifies for it.

$EXTERN Card, Get, Print, Prout;

$ENTRY Go {
  = <Prout 'c1.1.eof ' <Card>>
    <Prout 'c1.2.print-before'>
    <Prout 'c1.2.print-returns [' <Print 'P'> ']'>
    <Prout 'c1.3.prout-before'>
    <Prout 'c1.3.prout-returns [' <Prout 'Q'> ']'>
    <Prout 'c1.8.terminal [' <Get 0> ']'>;
}
